item('Dots: an always-on project steward','product','2026-09-29','https://openai.com/index/introducing-dots/','OpenAI describes persistent agents with their own cloud computer, browser, connected apps, parallel workstreams, and activity inspection.','The unit of automation becomes an owned workstream with memory and review.','Prototype a bounded project steward that maintains a decision log and returns reviewable artifacts.','Always-on agents force explicit scope, escalation, and evidence policies.','Access tiers may shift. Start with synthetic or low-risk data.','Run a 7-day steward experiment with approval checkpoints.'),
item('GPT-6.1 Sol: lower-cost long-horizon work','model','2026-09-29','https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-1-sol/','OpenAI positions GPT-6.1 Sol near Astra performance for coding, computer use, and professional workflows at roughly one-fifth the standard price.','Cheap context reuse changes the economics of agents that revisit project state.','Benchmark Buildn tasks by quality, retries, latency, and cost.','Model routing can now be governed by task difficulty and context reuse.','Benchmarks are vendor-reported. Reproduce them on your own acceptance set.','Run a 10-task before/after benchmark.'),
